# docs/ — Workflow Filesystem

This is the workflow filesystem for **{{ project_name }}**: where specs,
designs, decisions, testing notes, reviews, retrospectives, and archives live.

> **Note:** This structure was generated by the Copier foundation template at
> `tools/copier-foundation/`. Do not invent an alternative structure — extend
> this one. See [`decisions/0002-workflow-filesystem.md`](decisions/0002-workflow-filesystem.md)
> (if your project has adopted that ADR) for the source decision.

## Folders

| Folder | Purpose | Source of truth for |
|---|---|---|
| `current/` | Snapshot of current project state and active focus | "where are we now" |
| `milestones/` | Milestone status docs | milestone scope & status |
| `specs/` | Product / feature specifications | what to build |
| `design/` | UI page specs; `ui-prompts/` and `ui-integration-notes/` for UI work | UI intent & generator traceability |
| `decisions/` | Architecture Decision Records (ADRs), numbered `NNNN-title.md` | why a choice was made |
| `testing/` | Test plans, manual test notes, verification logs | test strategy |
| `review/` | Review notes and checklists | review outcomes |
| `retrospectives/` | Per-milestone retrospective notes | lessons learned |
| `archive/` | Superseded docs kept for history | historical record |

## Rules

- Delivery state (PRDs, epics, tasks) lives in your delivery workflow tool
  (e.g. CCPM under `.claude/`) and GitHub Issues — **not** here.
- UI issues must produce a Page Spec in `design/` before any UI-generator prompt.
- UI prompts go in `design/ui-prompts/`; integration notes in
  `design/ui-integration-notes/`.
- Decisions that affect architecture, tooling, or workflow get an ADR in
  `decisions/`.
